.TH DIGITS 1
.SH NAME
digits \- digit memory game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/digits
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Digits
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Games/Digits.HC
memory game.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A digit pattern is shown, then typed back; it grows by one digit each
time it is got right, and a wrong digit ends the round with two beeps and
the answer.
.PP
What the original is really demonstrating is the Define entry \- a list
of zero-terminated strings loaded into the symbol table under one name
and printed back with the
.B %Z
format code, which is how both the colour and its name come out of the
same list.  That list is
.BR ST_RAINBOW_10 :
BLACK, BROWN, RED, LTRED, YELLOW, GREEN, BLUE, PURPLE, LTGRAY, WHITE.
They are TempleOS's colour names, not the resistor code's, even though
the text calls them electrical engineering colour codes.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B space / Enter
Advance phase / restart after fail
.TP
.B 0-9
Guess next digit
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/digits.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
